# Why this file exists
#
# Git decides a file is binary by sniffing for a NUL byte in its first 8000 bytes, and it shows
# **no diff at all** for a file it calls binary. A generator script wrote a literal NUL into
# packages/core/src/cluster/cluster.ts during EPIC-011a, and that file was consequently invisible to
# two self-reviews — both of which reported coverage they did not have. The code was fine; the hole
# was in the review.
#
# `diff` forces a textual diff for these paths whatever their content, so a mistake like that shows
# up in review instead of hiding. `scripts/binary-files.mjs` is the other half: it fails the build so
# the NUL is removed rather than merely rendered.
#
# Deliberately `diff` rather than `text`. The `text` attribute normalises line endings on commit,
# and this repository commits fixtures whose exact bytes are the point — EPIC-010's corpus pins CRLF,
# lone CR and a byte-order mark on purpose. `diff` changes how git *shows* a file and never what it
# stores.

*.ts       diff
*.tsx      diff
*.js       diff
*.jsx      diff
*.mjs      diff
*.cjs      diff
*.json     diff
*.jsonc    diff
*.md       diff
*.css      diff
*.html     diff
*.sql      diff
*.sh       diff
*.yml      diff
*.yaml     diff
*.toml     diff
*.py       diff
*.txt      diff
*.license  diff
LICENSE    diff
NOTICE     diff
Dockerfile diff

# Committed fixtures exist to pin exact bytes: never normalise their line endings.
*.snap.txt -text diff

# Genuinely binary, and expected to be.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary
